# ── MARK LVI — what never belongs in the repository ──────────────────────────
# Everything listed here is created by the app on first run. A fresh clone with
# none of it present boots straight to the setup screen, which is the intended
# first experience — so nothing here needs to be committed, and some of it must
# never be.

# ── Secrets. Committing any of these publishes them. ──────────────────────────
# your Gemini API key, plus per-plugin credentials
config/api_keys.json
# rotated copies of it — the same secrets, kept by the config
# store's recovery walk
config/backups/
# the dashboard's TLS private key and certificate
config/certs/
# a LINKED WhatsApp session — committing it hands somebody
# your WhatsApp account, not just a key
config/whatsapp_web/
# Google OAuth tokens (Gmail / Calendar plugins)
**/token*.json
# Google OAuth client secrets
**/client_secret*.json
*credentials*.json
.env
.env.*

# ── Personal data the assistant accumulates about you ─────────────────────────
memory/long_term.json
# rotated backups of it, kept by the memory store's recovery walk
memory/backups/
memory/incidents.jsonl
memory/*.db
# phone-notification state (core/notify.py): subscription endpoints are
# per-device capability URLs, and the missed queue holds notification
# text — neither belongs in a repository
memory/push_subscriptions.json
memory/notify_queue.json
# plugin foundry staging (plugins/plugin_foundry.py): drafts ARIA generated
# that were not installed — including ones that failed validation — are
# working state, not code. Installed plugins live in plugins/ and ARE code.
memory/foundry/
# ALL runtime state under memory/ (2026-10-23 repo cleanup): the running
# app rewrites these constantly (semantic-memory embeddings, the code
# watcher's ledger, delegated-task records, scheduler state, saved
# routines) — operational data, never source. They were tracked once and
# the laptop's auto-commit kept publishing fresh snapshots to this public
# repo; untracked + ignored ends that. The memory/*.py modules are code
# and stay tracked — this rule names JSON only.
memory/*.json
memory/routines/*.json
# the consolidation pass's two Markdown files (core/consolidation.py):
# the resume card and the audit log are her working notes about the
# user — the .md extension is the only thing that would let them slip
# past the JSON rule above into the auto-commit.
memory/resume_card.md
memory/consolidation_log.md

# ── Python build noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# ── Virtual environments ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Editors and operating systems ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Runtime output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
logs/
downloads/
screenshots/

# ── Self-update sidecar state (updater.py) ─────────────────────────────
# Written by the app and the sidecar at runtime; the updater's own
# record must never be swept into the code it pulls.
memory/updater_state.json
memory/boot_stamp.json
memory/app_presence.json
memory/announce_drop.jsonl
memory/updater.lock
memory/update_hold
